{
  "name": "University Librarian elected new chair of Kenya body",
  "parent_id": 203313642253074,
  "group_id": "8cf7c406-2121-48be-8e31-fb7736940e2b",
  "alternates": [],
  "created_at": "2026-07-31T09:34:36.544Z",
  "deleted_at": null,
  "sort_by_date": null,
  "tag_list": [],
  "updated_at": "2026-07-31T09:34:36.624Z",
  "published_at": "2026-07-31T09:34:36.611Z",
  "id": 203984390363000,
  "uuid": "56ad4e29-e724-4cda-96dc-ce5cc8cfeb5b",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "00970235-eaae-1b02-94fe-000012bf67ce",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "18a3b1e9-4755-2ee6-d545-210cac5dd969",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"I am humbled and excited to serve as the new Chairperson of KLA. I thank the outcoming team for their commitment to libraries and challenge the new team to embrace the spirit of servant leadership,\" he said. \"As we face an uncertain future, I am ready to work with all of you to strengthen our association and support our early career librarians.\" ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The conference discussions revolved around integrating libraries with modern technologies in their daily operations. This means a change in how traditional libraries run to enhance efficiency in knowledge management. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"As the incoming Chairperson, I will fast-track the establishment of the Kenya Library Association Bill and develop a continuous professional development framework for Librarians in Kenya. I will also work towards modelling best practices for libraries in Kenya at national, regional and county levels.\" ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Prof Gatiti oversees 12 libraries in AKU's global network dispersed in six countries. His research interests include information sciences, systemic reviews, evidence-based practice, bibliometric analysis and knowledge management. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"Libraries are better placed in terms of aligning research agenda with immerging themes such as SDGs, competency-based curriculum, climate change, and mental health, among others. This will become a reality under my leadership of the association.\" ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Prof Gatiti is currently leading a team of AKU researchers in implementing a Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights repository, a project funded by the World Health Organization. ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
